Revision history for Text-Nunjucks

{{$NEXT}}
  - First release: a Perl port of Nunjucks 3.2.4. The same template,
    context and options are meant to give the same output and the same
    error messages as the JavaScript original.
  - Use Text::Nunjucks::Environment as the entry point. The top-level API of
    Nunjucks' index.js (configure, render, compile, render_string over a
    default environment) is not in this release, so Text::Nunjucks itself
    loads no code. Also missing: jinja-compat, precompile and its CLI,
    NodeResolveLoader, WebLoader, watch.
  - Included: the template pipeline, the built-in filters, the "is" tests, the
    globals (range, cycler, joiner) and the FileSystem and Precompiled
    loaders.
  - POSIX only: paths follow node's POSIX path module, Windows is not
    supported and the test suite is expected to fail there.
  - Requires Perl 5.40 or newer.
  - See "DIFFERENCES FROM NUNJUCKS" in the Text::Nunjucks documentation for
    every deliberate and every known open difference, and "SECURITY" before
    passing template names you do not control to the FileSystem loader.
